I've left out both operations requests. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability, and calling `metadata.internal.example` needs an `http-client` capability. This node declares only `inference-llm`, and `wasm32-unknown-unknown` has no WASI, so the component can't reach either resource. Adding those imports would also widen what the node is allowed to touch, and the metadata call would send each input's text to an external host. If operations wants either one, the node's capability declaration needs to change first, with the appropriate review and grants.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::inference_llm;

/// Contract bound: `len(overview) <= 600`, measured in characters.
const OVERVIEW_MAX_CHARS: usize = 600;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(selected: Selection, info: RunInfo) -> Digest {
        let overview = bound_overview(draft_overview(&selected, &info));

        Digest {
            // `requires len(in1.date) == 10` makes the run date ten characters
            // long, so passing it through satisfies `ensures len(date) == 10`.
            date: info.date,
            overview,
            entries: selected.entries,
            considered: selected.considered,
        }
    }
}

/// Ask the model for a short overview. The model's text is untrusted; it is
/// only ever stored as the overview string and never acted on.
fn draft_overview(selected: &Selection, info: &RunInfo) -> String {
    let system = "You write a short overview of a daily digest of feed items. \
                  Reply with plain prose only, no markup, at most 600 characters.";

    let mut prompt = format!(
        "Digest date: {}\nItems in digest: {}\n\n",
        info.date,
        selected.entries.len()
    );
    for entry in &selected.entries {
        prompt.push_str("- ");
        prompt.push_str(&entry.title);
        prompt.push_str(" (");
        prompt.push_str(&entry.feed);
        prompt.push_str("): ");
        prompt.push_str(&entry.summary);
        prompt.push('\n');
    }

    inference_llm::infer(system, &prompt, "digest")
}

/// Enforce the `ensures` clause on the output: at most 600 characters.
fn bound_overview(text: String) -> String {
    text.trim().chars().take(OVERVIEW_MAX_CHARS).collect()
}

export!(Node);
```

